{
 "v": 1,
 "about": "The Rig. Symbols in ring order: hat, saucer, dish, eye, moon, lizard (a Nudge step moves round this ring, wrapping). Paytable (x bet): three Hats 20, other three of a kind 8, a pair of Hats 4, another pair 1, else 0. Order: honest reels -> reel cards in slot order (each sees the reels the previous left; a muted card is skipped) -> the Nudge -> paytable on the final reels -> payout cards in slot order, every multiplier card first, then Skim -> payout never below 0. A re-roll takes ONE value from draws (0-4) = that index among the five symbols other than the excluded one, in ring order. touched = the step changed the reels (reel card) or the payout (payout card); bit = the step lowered the payout (reel card: the paytable on the reels before vs after its step). Rake: only when payout < bet and something bit: bet - payout split evenly over the cards that bit (whole chips; remainder to the bank); else a loss goes to the bank and a win/push is paid by the bank (bank_delta: + = the bank gains). history = earlier spins of this round, oldest first (their final result + final reels).",
